---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {techProjects} from '../../data/tech-projects';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '') + '/';
---
<Layout title="How I Build & Verify Projects — ICY TECH" description="A practical look at design decisions, testing, deployment and the evidence behind my independent engineering projects.">
  <section class="tech-shell tech-hero">
    <p class="tech-eyebrow">Engineering practice</p>
    <h1>Build it.<br /><em>Test it.</em><br />Make it useful.</h1>
    <p class="tech-lead">My projects combine application development, AI integration, creative interfaces and local infrastructure. I focus on systems people can understand, test and improve—not just prototypes that look finished.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="tech-shell tech-section">
    <h2>How I approach engineering</h2>
    <div class="tech-grid">
      <article class="tech-card">
        <h3>Start with the problem</h3>
        <p>Define the workflow, the user's decisions and the data that must survive. Then choose tools suited to the work—whether that's a web interface, a Python API or a local service.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tech-card">
        <h3>Test real behavior</h3>
        <p>Use automated tests, browser checks, reproducible inputs and direct inspection. Different kinds of testing answer different questions, so each project records what was actually exercised.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tech-card">
        <h3>Build for changes and failures</h3>
        <p>Separate original data from derived results, make important actions recoverable and keep permissions explicit. A system should remain understandable when something goes wrong.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="tech-shell tech-section">
    <h2>Explore the implementations</h2>
    <p class="tech-lead">These are starting points for seeing the architecture, code-level choices and demonstrations behind the work.</p>
    <div class="tech-grid">
      {techProjects.slice(0,6).map(project => <article class="tech-card">
        <p class="tech-eyebrow">{project.category}</p>
        <h3><a href={base + 'projects/' + project.slug + '/'}>{project.name}</a></h3>
        <p>{project.summary}</p>
        <div class="tech-linkrow"><a href={base + 'projects/' + project.slug + '/'}>View project →</a></div>
      </article>)}
    </div>
    <p class="tech-linkrow"><a class="tech-button" href={base + 'projects/'}>Explore all projects →</a><a href="https://github.com/icyNatural" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub profile ↗</a></p>
  </section>
</Layout>
